-- PAPER-LEARN-PROBATION-SETTLE-1 part 9 of 9 (2026-11-05, charter pillar autonomy, program QNFO.OPS; cluster C8-PROJECTS-GOALS of the roadmap and backlog completion sweep).
-- Settles 25 probationary direct paper learnings (ids 6048 to 6280 of the 225 read on 2026-11-04 23:00Z): each row was read in full (claim, lever, application and the model's apply signal) against the live fleet and given one disposition with its reason.
-- PAPER-LEARN-TRIAGE-1 parked them in probation because its catalogue held 6 mechanisms; the apply signal usually meant the model did not know the fleet already does this. Dispositions: already-in-place (mechanism named, existence read today), rejected (category and specific reason, with what would justify re-proposing), routed (to agent_issues 1000459 TRIGGER-FLAP-1 or goal external-impact-per-dollar).
-- Each goal PAPER-LEARN-<id> (DoD: the learning is settled) then completes on its next probe, and roadmap row GL-PAPER-LEARN-<id> verifies in the hourly loop. Revert one row: UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'probation' WHERE id = <id>.
-- APPLY-BY: ci
-- DB: qnfo-audit
-- Rollback: UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = (SELECT b.fleet_status FROM bak_20261105_c8_pl_09 b WHERE b.id = paper_learnings.id), status_note = (SELECT b.status_note FROM bak_20261105_c8_pl_09 b WHERE b.id = paper_learnings.id), updated_at = (SELECT b.updated_at FROM bak_20261105_c8_pl_09 b WHERE b.id = paper_learnings.id) WHERE id IN (SELECT id FROM bak_20261105_c8_pl_09)

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS bak_20261105_c8_pl_09 AS SELECT * FROM paper_learnings WHERE id IN (6048, 6076, 6077, 6078, 6079, 6080, 6081, 6105, 6110, 6134, 6135, 6136, 6137, 6150, 6151, 6152, 6154, 6231, 6232, 6233, 6238, 6276, 6277, 6278, 6280);

UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'already-in-place', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 in place (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; modeleval): Model-pairing and steering decisions rest on measurement, not assumed overlap factors: qnfo-model-eval benchmarks candidates against the production control on a fixed battery, and ENSEMBLE-POLICY-1 requires disjoint families whose actual agreement is observed (a 9-judge, 7-family panel is worth about 2.2 votes).', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 6048 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'already-in-place', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 in place (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; blocked): A compliant blocked state exists: contract verdicts include deferred and escalated, a run that cannot proceed is recorded as skipped or failed with its reason in fleet_runs, and CLAIM-UNREACHABLE-FALLBACK-1 states that an unreachable claim service records a verbatim error and the work continues.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 6076 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'rejected', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 rejected (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; no-measured-gap): Blocked-invocation exposure 1-(1-q)^n is the paper''s worked example. Fleet runs record failed and refused calls directly (fleet_runs, cron-watch fault views, orphan reaping), so exposure is measured per task rather than derived from assumed q and n. Re-propose with a loop whose measured exposure disagreed with the product.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 6077 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'rejected', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 rejected (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; no-measured-gap): The (2/3)^k completeness gap belongs to the paper''s three-state tool model; no fleet rule is shown to have halted a loop through binary use-or-forbidden phrasing. Re-propose with a halt traced to such a rule.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 6078 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'rejected', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 rejected (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; analogy-only): Undecidability of compliant halting concerns arbitrary protocols; fleet rules change by pull request under canary, review gate and revert, which does not depend on proving halt-freedom. Re-propose with a doctrine amendment that deadlocked a loop.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 6079 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'already-in-place', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 in place (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; blocker): A claim of blocked needs evidence: CLAUDE.md requires the attempt to be made and recorded in blocker_redteam with a verdict (false-belief-removed, workaround-built or confirmed-with-evidence plus the refusal text), and unverified_blocker_claims (36) lists claims nobody tested.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 6080 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'already-in-place', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 in place (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; invalidclass): Why a loop stalled is classified: DEPLOY-PROBES-1 separates DEPLOY-PROBE-REVERTED-1 (a regression) from DEPLOY-PROBE-FAILED-1 (pre-existing, mistyped marker or inconclusive), and distinct ticket families name refusals (CODE-MERGE-REFUSED-1, CODE-LOOP-EXHAUSTED-1, PROBE-NEEDED-1).', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 6081 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'already-in-place', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 in place (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; ens): Ensemble members are chosen from disjoint model families so a shared base does not make the check correlated (ENSEMBLE-POLICY-1; REVIEW-GATE-1 uses two disjoint families).', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 6105 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'already-in-place', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 in place (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; bands): Gate thresholds are set empirically with margins: warning_band and kill_band are held for 333 and 257 of 418 metrics, and METRIC-CLOSED-LOOP-1 replaces a threshold or remedy that did not move its metric within 7 days.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 6110 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'already-in-place', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 in place (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; independent): Cross-checks use independent inputs: a risky diff is read by two disjoint model families, probes read live state rather than the artifact''s own table, and the verify stage recomputes from the paper''s stated inputs with another family.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 6134 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'already-in-place', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 in place (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; independent): Authoring and verifying a metric by one loop is not accepted as trust: remediation probes run in qnfo-fleet-control and the consumer, the lane (not the author) merges, and v_trust_ledger counts verified outcomes only.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 6135 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'rejected', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 rejected (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; no-measured-gap): Setting a trigger at the boundary between competing diagnoses is the paper''s statistical design for its own account. Fleet triggers carry a per-metric breach cause (metric_breach_cause) and a lever, and no diagnosis is shown to have been drawn from a breach set below its discriminating bound. Re-propose with one.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 6136 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'already-in-place', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 in place (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; invariants): Cross-artifact contradictions are detected and filed: v_issue_accounting, the fleet graph drift findings, mirror-guard and version-bump-guard compare declared with live state and file findings or fail the pull request.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 6137 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'rejected', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 rejected (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; analogy-only): The prime counting asymptotic is mathematics, not a workload model; no fleet loop schedules work from prime counts. Re-propose with a loop whose workload is a function of a number-theoretic quantity.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 6150 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'rejected', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 rejected (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; analogy-only): The Legendre-sieve inflation of the prime counting error term is the paper''s result; no fleet alert monitors such an error term.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 6151 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'rejected', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 rejected (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; analogy-only): A syntactic functoriality test for first-order statement transfer concerns the paper''s formal language; the fleet merges code and migrations, not lemmas, and gates them with pr-checks, the review gate and deploy probes.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 6152 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'rejected', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 rejected (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; analogy-only): Presentation-level constants such as the twin-prime correlation constant are number theory; the budget optimizer uses no such constant, only measured spend. Re-propose with a budget rule that used a number-theoretic constant.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 6154 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'routed', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 routed (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; trigger-flap): Routed to agent_issues 1000459 (TRIGGER-FLAP-1, open, critical, qnfo-fleet-control): expressing a breach in units of the metric''s own spread (a band around its rolling mean instead of a bare absolute threshold) is the fix that issue applies to tickets closing and reopening in a loop (167 reopens on 44 tickets in 7 days).', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 6231 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'rejected', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 rejected (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; duplicate): Duplicate of learning 6231 (routed to agent_issues 1000459, TRIGGER-FLAP-1): triggering on mean over spread or spread over mean is a variant of the same normalized-band lever, and that issue picks the band form from the measured reopen data.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 6232 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'rejected', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 rejected (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; duplicate): Duplicate of learning 6231 (routed to agent_issues 1000459, TRIGGER-FLAP-1): a log-scale band for multiplicative quantities is a variant of the same normalized-band lever; spend caps themselves are dollar values in fleet_budget.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 6233 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'rejected', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 rejected (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; duplicate): Duplicate of learning 6231 (routed to agent_issues 1000459, TRIGGER-FLAP-1): eligibility of a metric for a spread-normalized trigger is a condition of that same lever and is decided there with the measured reopen data.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 6238 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'already-in-place', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 in place (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; relapse): A zero-failure reading does not close an issue on its own: the close hold (migrations/2026-11-04-relapse-hold-1.sql, v_issue_close_hold) requires the passes since the last reopen or failure to span 20 to 120 minutes by relapse history, and a closed issue whose contract fails again is reopened.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 6276 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'rejected', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 rejected (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; no-measured-gap): No fleet rule demands empirical confirmation of a small failure-rate claim, which is the paper''s quantum-error-correction situation; the fleet''s equivalent is the relapse hold above, set from measured reopen data. Re-propose with a fleet claim that demanded more trials than could be run.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 6277 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'already-in-place', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 in place (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; ens): Checker independence is the stated condition: ENSEMBLE-POLICY-1 notes that a 9-judge, 7-family panel is worth about 2.2 votes because errors are correlated, requires disjoint families, and keeps non-model layers (deterministic gate, reader votes, owner verdict).', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 6278 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'rejected', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 rejected (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; paper-convention): Pre-registered observable violations for each hypothesis are this paper''s own practice for its error-correction proposal; making them a registered metric for every pipeline hypothesis is a new hard gate with no measured defect. Re-propose with the share of published hypotheses that state no refutation.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 6280 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
